#519 sgirandomcolour -- PRE-TABLE CHECK for KILL TABLE 3 (the pass-3 closure of M13/M14).
Written 2026-09-10 by the Opus 5 measuring seat, BEFORE table 3's first build.  Its mtime is the
proof of order; the frozen instrument, frozen baseline and frozen driver are all stamped after it.

Instrument under review: regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py, uncommitted, this round's own
deliverable.  Diff under review: NONE -- src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c is UNTOUCHED by this pass.  Table 3
scores a DETECTOR change, not a product change, which is why the (b) and (c) legs matter as much as
the (d) ones: they are what proves the enlarged instrument still discriminates on the axes it
already covered.

*** WHAT THIS PASS EXISTS FOR.  `M13_widthdecline' (ok = 0 -> if (bufdepth == 4) ok = 0;) and
`M14_lineardecline' (-> if (linear) ok = 0;) scored 14/14 on the table-1 instrument and 19/19 on the
19-row one -- TWO MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPES.  Both are UNDER-declining clause-(d) mutants: where the
added condition is false the unsupported colour type is PERMITTED and the guarded store runs, and
because #519 deleted the random() fill that store now writes UNINITIALISED buf. ***

0. THE PRESCRIPTION WAS CHECKED BEFORE IT WAS IMPLEMENTED, AND IT IS CORRECT
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The 18-cell table came from a design review, not a measurement, and this round has already had
   one premise (the mutants' DIRECTION) measured backwards.  Every element was re-derived from
   src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c and then MEASURED with a throwaway probe against the fix binary
   (o519_explore.py / o519_explore2.py; logs preserved as EXPLORE_*.out beside this file).

   FIELD ARITHMETIC, from horrible_getputpixel's own first four lines:
       color_mode = mode & DE_MODE_TYPE_MASK      (0x00f0)
       bufdepth   = 1 << ((mode >> 8) & 3)        (bits 9:8 -> 1, 2, 4, 8)
       tlb_mode   = (mode >> 10) & 0x7            (bits 12:10)
       linear     = tlb_mode > 3
   The three fields are disjoint, so a mode word sets all three independently.

       mode    tlb_mode  label    bufdepth  type    bufdepth==4 || linear
       0x0000     0      TLB_A       1      CI      false
       0x0210     0      TLB_A       4      RGB     true
       0x0220     0      TLB_A       4      RGBA    true
       0x0230     0      TLB_A       4      ABGR    true
       0x00f0     0      TLB_A       1      YCRCB   FALSE   <- the corner
       0x0400     1      TLB_B       1      CI      false
       0x0610/20/30  1   TLB_B       4      RGB/RGBA/ABGR    true
       0x04f0     1      TLB_B       1      YCRCB   FALSE   <- the corner
       0x0800     2      TLB_C       1      CI      false
       0x0a10/20/30  2   TLB_C       4      RGB/RGBA/ABGR    true
       0x08f0     2      TLB_C       1      YCRCB   FALSE   <- the corner
       0x12f0     4      LIN_A       4      YCRCB   true    (every declined row shipped so far)

   ALL THREE PRESCRIBED CLAIMS HOLD:
     * the TLB_B and TLB_C mode words are right -- 0x0400/0x0800 select tlb_mode 1/2 and leave
       bits 9:8 zero, and 0x06x0/0x0ax0 add BUFDEPTH_32 without disturbing the label field;
     * 0x00f0 really is depth-1, TILED and YCRCB simultaneously;
     * the corner really does make BOTH added conditions false, so it is exactly the cell M13 and
       M14 permit.
   MEASURED on the fix binary: every accept cell returned its prescribed word at all three windows
   (0xdd223344 / 0xaabbcc00 / 0xaabbccdd / 0xddccbbaa) and every declined cell returned the paint
   0x11223344, with exactly ONE announce carrying `[ put: color mode = 0xf0 ]'.  `unimplemented
   dst_mode' appears ZERO times, so the tiled mode words reach the COLOUR switch and not the
   TLB/mode default.

   TWO THINGS THE PRESCRIPTION DID NOT SAY, both measured rather than argued:
   (a) THE TILED ADDRESS.  setup_put() programs RE_LINEAR_A; the tiled path takes tileptr from
       re_tlb_[abc][tile_nr] << 16 and needs BIT 15 of the stored halfword set (it becomes
       tileptr's bit 31, the "valid" bit).  One 8-byte store fills four entries from big-endian
       halfwords, so `sd 0x8001000000000000' at CRIME_RE_TLB_A gives re_tlb_a[0] = 0x8001 and a
       destination of physical 0x10000.  The three windows are given DIFFERENT tiles -- 0x8001,
       0x8002, 0x8003 -> phys 0x10000/0x20000/0x30000 -- so an accept cell pins WHICH array the
       mode word selected (clause (f) anchoring), not merely that a write happened somewhere.
   (b) THE OFFSET.  At (0,0) every cell here has ofs 0, so the review's (4,1) arithmetic
       (512*1 + 4 = 516 at tiled depth 1) is correct but not exercised: the position axis stays
       pinned by the existing `ycrcb x4y1' row on the LINEAR path.

1. SIBLING PARITY
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Unchanged from table 1's block: the PUT default arm's sibling is the GET default arm (untouched,
   disclosed as sgirebufuninit) and the TLB/mode switch's own default (SGIRE_W_BADMODE), which
   RETURNS before the store.  N/A for this pass in one respect and the reason is recorded rather
   than left blank: NO PRODUCT CODE CHANGES IN PASS 3, so there is no new arm to compare against a
   sibling.  What this pass adds is coverage of arms that already existed.
   NEW SIBLING SET, and it is the reason for three sessions rather than one: the FOUR dispatch
   labels that reach the guarded store -- TLB_A, TLB_B, TLB_C, LIN_A.  Before this pass the
   declined rows drove ONE of them.  A parity census over the row names was the check that would
   have shown that, and it is what section 5 now does over the whole 4x4 domain.

2. CLAIM -> ROW  (every added comment sentence that asserts an observable consequence)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   "all sixteen cells ... are driven with an unsupported colour type and a readback"
                                            -> the sixteen declined cells themselves; negative
                                               controls M20..M27
   "an accept cell pins WHICH array the mode word selected"
                                            -> tA/tB/tC ci8|rgb|rgba|abgr (12 cells), each reading
                                               its own window's distinct tile
   "a latch or an announce conditioned on the addressing mode"
                                            -> tA/tB/tC silent | ann1 | ann cum (9 rows)
   "a SECOND declined PUT here, latch already set, still skips its store"
                                            -> tA/tB/tC ycrcb rpt (3 rows)
   "the primitive fires synchronously inside the second store"
                                            -> NO ROW, and none is owed: it is a statement about
                                               why the readback in the same stepped block is valid.
                                               Its negative control is that every accept cell would
                                               read the paint if it were false.
   "0x8001 is not decoration: 0x0001 returns without writing"
                                            -> NO ROW.  SENTENCE, carried from sgi_re_rgb_probe.py's
                                               own measured note; no cell here drives a clear bit 15.
   "measured for every cell ... never assumed"  -> section 6 below IS that measurement.

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Guard (the predicate that decides the decline): `color_mode', a local derived from `mode'.
   Guarded BODY: cpu->memory_rw(cpu, cpu->mem, tileptr + ofs, buf, bufdepth, MEM_WRITE, ...).
   Body-read lvalues: tileptr, ofs, buf, bufdepth, cpu->mem.
     tileptr  <- assigned by the switch on tlb_mode  (case 0/1/2 from re_tlb_[abc], case 4 from
                 re_linear_a).  So tlb_mode's value FLOWS INTO a body-read lvalue: by the
                 2026-09-09 dispatch-label ruling it is a FLOOR AXIS of this guard.
     ofs      <- 512*y + (x % tilewidth)*bufdepth on the tiled path, x & 4095 on the linear one.
                 Depends on BOTH tlb_mode and bufdepth.
     bufdepth <- passed straight to the store as its LENGTH.
     buf      <- written by the four supported arms and NOT by the default arm.  THE DISAGREEING
                 STATE the rule asks for is therefore "the store runs with buf unassigned", which
                 is precisely what a permitting mutant produces -- and section 6 measures what
                 lands.
   WHERE GUARD AND BODY DISAGREE: `color_mode' is written nowhere the body reads.  So a decline
   conditioned on color_mode is invisible to any body-side oracle and is coverage debt, not floor
   -- disclosed in the contract with M28 as its negative control.

4. CHANNEL -- per row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs under it
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   tA/tB/tC ycrcb d1   M13_widthdecline, M15_jointwidthlin, M24_permit_d2d8,
                       M20/M21/M22 (the one that exempts THIS label)      -> word != paint
   tA/tB/tC ycrcb d2   M13, M15, M26_permit_d2                            -> word != paint
   tA/tB/tC ycrcb d4   M14_lineardecline, M23_permit_tiled_d4             -> word != paint
   tA/tB/tC ycrcb d8   M13, M15, M25_permit_d8, M24                       -> word != paint
   lin ycrcb d1/d2/d8  M13, M24, M25, M26 on the LINEAR label             -> word != paint
   tA/tB/tC ycrcb rpt  M4_okinlatch at a tiled window                     -> word != paint
   tA/tB/tC ci8|rgb|rgba|abgr
                       M8_declineall; M9/M16/M17/M10 (the case dropped);
                       any window-conditioned case drop                   -> word != expected packing
   tA/tB/tC silent     an announce moved to the accept side               -> count > 0
   tA/tB/tC ann1       a latch or announce conditioned on tlb_mode;
                       M7_silent                                          -> count 0
   tA/tB/tC ann cum    M5_nolatch at a tiled window                        -> count > 1
   lin ann cum         M5_nolatch on the linear label                      -> count > 1

   *** VACUOUS-BY-CONSTRUCTION AUDIT.  A row whose named channel cannot vary under its named
   mutant is vacuous, and that is knowable BEFORE the table.  Two findings: ***
     * `tA ycrcb d4' does NOT vary under M13 (bufdepth == 4 is true there, so M13 declines and the
       paint stands).  It is not vacuous -- it varies under M14 and M23 -- but it is NOT a control
       for M13 and must not be reported as one.
     * `tA/tB/tC silent' and the accept cells cannot vary under ANY of M13/M14/M15/M20..M27: those
       mutants only widen what is PERMITTED, and permitting cannot make an accept cell wrong.  They
       are declared CONTROLS for this family, not detectors of it, exactly as `indep paint' was
       declared a control for `latch indep' in table 1's block.

5. THE (d) ENUMERATION FOR TABLE 3, and it is stated over a DOMAIN rather than a mutant list
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The repair-chain amendment says that when two consecutive passes find breaches of one class, the
   next repair owes the CLASS CLOSURE: enumerate the full space from the function's own inputs and
   close every cell in ONE diff.  This pass does that.

   Reachable-to-the-store partition of tlb_mode: {0 TLB_A, 1 TLB_B, 2 TLB_C, 4 LIN_A}.  3 and 5-7
   take the BADMODE default, which RETURNS before the store; >= 8 is impossible after `& 0x7'.
   Domain of bufdepth: exactly {1, 2, 4, 8} -- `1 << ((mode >> 8) & 3)'.
   The 4 x 4 = 16 declined cells:

       label \ depth      1        2        4        8
       TLB_A            0x00f0   0x01f0   0x02f0   0x03f0
       TLB_B            0x04f0   0x05f0   0x06f0   0x07f0
       TLB_C            0x08f0   0x09f0   0x0af0   0x0bf0
       LIN_A            0x10f0   0x11f0   0x12f0*  0x13f0      (* the ONE cell already shipped)

   With all sixteen present in the declined set, NO predicate over tlb_mode and bufdepth alone can
   be false at every declined cell -- whatever its shape, because the declined set is the entire
   reachable domain of those two lvalues.  That is a stronger claim than "these mutant forms die",
   and M20..M27 are its negative controls rather than its content.

   MUTANTS, one edit each, all dry-run to exactly one match (o519_dryrun.sh output preserved):
     floor (b)  M1_reinstate           the pre-fix arm verbatim inside the new structure
     floor (c)  M11_null               the pre-fix file wholesale (also serves clause (a):
                                       it is byte-identical to HEAD's dev_sgi_re.c)
     floor (d)  M2_noguard  M3_zerofill  M4_okinlatch
                M13_widthdecline       if (bufdepth == 4)      ** MUST NOW DIE **
                M14_lineardecline      if (linear)             ** MUST NOW DIE **
                M15_jointwidthlin      if (bufdepth == 4 || linear)
                M20_permit_tlba        if (tlb_mode != 0)      permits TLB_A only
                M21_permit_tlbb        if (tlb_mode != 1)
                M22_permit_tlbc        if (tlb_mode != 2)
                M23_permit_tiled_d4    if (linear || bufdepth != 4)
                M24_permit_d2d8        if (bufdepth == 1 || bufdepth == 4)
                M25_permit_d8          if (bufdepth != 8)
                M26_permit_d2          if (bufdepth != 2)
                M27_permit_bc_d2d8     if (tlb_mode == 0 || linear || bufdepth == 1
                                           || bufdepth == 4)  -- the 4-term joint that the
                                       PREVIOUS (10-cell) plan would have left open
     latch      M5_nolatch  M6_sharedbit  M7_silent
     accept     M8_declineall  M9_dropcase_ci  M10_dropcase_abgr  M16_dropcase_rgb
                M17_dropcase_rgba
     L4         M12_prefix_reworded
     BOUNDARY   M28_permit_othernibbles  if (color_mode == 0xf0 || color_mode == 0x50)
                                       -- PREDICTED TO ESCAPE.  Disclosed in the contract, and it
                                       is clause-(e) debt rather than a floor breach because
                                       color_mode does not flow into any body-read lvalue.

6. THE CAUTION THE BRIEF ASKED ME TO TEST RATHER THAN REPEAT -- AND IT IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   "unchanged paint does not prove absence of a store: at depth 1, an erroneous byte equal to 0x11
   passes."  TRUE IN PRINCIPLE, and the whole declined half of this instrument rests on it, so it
   was measured before any row was written -- by building M13 and reading what a PERMITTED store
   actually puts there.

   MEASURED, by building M13_widthdecline and M15_jointwidthlin in the clone and running the
   throwaway explorer against each (EXPLORE_M13.out, EXPLORE_M15.out, preserved beside this file;
   the fix binary's own run is EXPLORE_BASE.out).  Destination pre-painted 0x11223344 everywhere:

       cell (TLB_A)      fix        M13_widthdecline   M15_jointwidthlin
       0x00f0  d1     0x11223344      0x70223344         0x70223344
       0x01f0  d2     0x11223344      0x70633344         0x70633344
       0x02f0  d4     0x11223344      0x11223344         0x11223344   (both DECLINE here)
       0x03f0  d8     0x11223344      0x7063000f         0x70630017
       0x00f0  rpt    0x11223344      0x70223344         0x70223344
       (TLB_B and TLB_C d1 and rpt: identical, 0x70223344 under both mutants)

   SO: A PERMITTED STORE AT DEPTH 1 WRITES 0x70, NOT 0x11.  No cell of the eighteen -- nor of the
   twenty-four this pass actually ships -- is vacuous for the stated reason.  THE VALUE IS
   MEASURED, NOT GUARANTEED, and three things about it are worth recording because they bound how
   far the measurement can be trusted:
     * buf[0] = 0x70 and buf[1] = 0x63 are STABLE across two different binaries (M13 and M15) and
       across all three windows and both the first and the repeated PUT -- so it is a deterministic
       stack residue, not noise;
     * buf[2..3] are NOT stable: 0x000f under M13 and 0x0017 under M15.  A cell whose kill rests on
       the LOW bytes of a depth-8 store would be build-dependent.  Every cell here is killed by
       byte 0, which is the stable one;
     * the residue is still UNINITIALISED STACK by construction.  If some future build put 0x11
       there, the depth-1 cells would go silently green.  The instrument is not defenceless against
       that: the depth-2 cell requires 0x70,0x63 == 0x11,0x22 and the depth-8 cell requires four
       bytes to coincide, so the SET of cells degrades gracefully where any single cell could not.
       That is the honest statement -- collectively robust, individually contingent -- and it is
       why the contract discloses it as (iv) rather than claiming the cells are unconditional.

   AND THE ANNOUNCE IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE ORACLE, which is what makes the readback load-bearing:
   under BOTH permitting mutants the announce still fires exactly once with the right text.  A
   detector built only on the announce would score M13 and M14 CLEAN, which is precisely how they
   escaped 14/14 and 19/19.

7. APPARATUS DEFECTS FOUND IN MY OWN INSTRUMENTS WHILE DOING THIS, RECORDED RATHER THAN QUIETLY
   FIXED -- all three are classes the carrier already names
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   a. A MARKER GREP THAT MATCHED NOTHING REPORTED 0 FOR EVERYTHING.  The first explorer split the
      transcript on "0x00519519"; the debugger prints "0x519519", so the split never happened and
      the fallback string was counted instead -- giving `announce before marker = 0' and
      `between markers = 0' as CONFIDENT, WRONG measurements of a string literal.  Caught only
      because the same block printed `marker1 seen=False' beside the counts.  THE DENOMINATOR RULE
      WORKING: a count printed without a "did the selector select anything" companion is not
      evidence.  The corrected run gives 0 before / 1 between / 1 total, which is what the
      prescription asked for.
   b. THE BASH -> HEREDOC -> PYTHON BACKSLASH COLLAPSE, in the direction the carrier documents.
      mut519c.py's find-strings for M1_reinstate and M7_silent quote a fatal() whose format ends
      "]\n".  Written as a doubled backslash in a quoted heredoc, one level was consumed, Python
      read a REAL NEWLINE, and both mutants reported MUTANT-TEXT-NOT-FOUND -- the presence-pin
      firing correctly on a defect in the mutator rather than in the tree.  Repaired with chr(92),
      which is immune in both directions, and re-dry-run: all 25 mutants now apply with exactly one
      match each.
   c. I EDITED THE MUTATOR WHILE THE PRE-CHECK WAS STILL RUNNING.  Adding M28 to mut519c.py at
      ~16:07 landed between the pre-check's M13 leg and its M15 leg, and a multi-run driver
      re-reads its mutator between legs.  The edit adds one dictionary entry and changes no
      find/replace string -- verified by re-running the dry run -- so M15's mutation is unaffected,
      but the hazard is exactly the one this project records, and the pre-check is therefore NOT a
      frozen-instrument measurement.  TABLE 3 IS: it runs from frozen copies of the instrument, the
      mutator, the baseline and the driver, all stamped after this file.

8. WHAT IS N/A HERE, WITH ITS REASON -- an unrun check and an inapplicable one must not render the
   same
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   * ACCEPT-ROW FAILABILITY (the de-escalation companion): N/A for this pass in its own right --
     it binds a round that REMOVES a host-fatal guard, and pass 3 changes no product code.  The
     obligation was discharged in the fix's own pass and its rows (`live', `ci8 put', `rgb put',
     `abgr put') are re-scored here unchanged, joined by twelve more at the tiled windows.
   * ORACLE CORRECTION (re-pin first, measure red, then change code): N/A -- no shipped oracle is
     re-pinned.  Every existing row keeps its expectation byte for byte; the pass only ADDS.
   * PROPAGATION TO BUILD TREES: N/A -- the only file changed is a probe, and probes do not live in
     the build trees.  src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c is untouched, so build/, build-asan/,
     /tmp/gxsec-build and est/ are all unaffected by this pass and none of them was written.

9. ORDER OF OPERATIONS, so the record is checkable rather than asserted
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   explorer runs (BASE/M13/M15)  ->  THIS FILE  ->  freeze instrument+mutator+baseline+driver  ->
   table 3 leg 1 (BASE).  The explorer runs precede this file deliberately: the CHANNEL check is
   only worth anything if it is MEASURED, and section 6 is that measurement.  Table 3 itself has
   not started when this file is written, and every artifact it produces is stamped later.
